3. THE SQL LANGUAGE AND THE COMPANION TEXT
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

   Kwery implements the SQL language as standardised in ISO/IEC 9075, and where
   the standard leaves a choice it behaves as PostgreSQL does. Its engine, its
   views and its teaching material were written from scratch.

   The lessons follow the chapter order and the terms of "Database System
   Concepts" by Abraham Silberschatz, Henry F. Korth and S. Sudarshan (7th
   edition, McGraw-Hill, 2019), which is cited as the companion text. The
   sample databases, their data, and all text, figures, examples and
   exercises are Kwery's own; none is taken from the book.


